    <h2 style="color:#0f1f3d;margin-top:32px;">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What battery standard does the UAE use for trucks?</h3>
      <p>The UAE runs a premium European-heavy fleet (Mercedes-Benz, Volvo, Scania, MAN, DAF, Iveco) alongside a Japanese and Asian segment (Hino, Isuzu, Tata, Ashok Leyland), so JIS N150/N200 and DIN88/DIN100 batteries are both common. Match the battery to the vehicle's group and voltage.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Why is humidity as important as heat for batteries in the UAE?</h3>
      <p>Coastal UAE combines summer temperatures of 40°C+ with high humidity from the Persian Gulf. Heat accelerates lead-acid ageing and water loss, while humidity and salt air promote terminal corrosion. Correct electrolyte care and corrosion-resistant terminals matter more here than inland.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>What certification does a battery need to enter the UAE?</h3>
      <p>The UAE requires an Emirates Conformity Assessment Scheme (ECAS) certificate or Emirates Quality Mark (EQM) for regulated products, administered by the Ministry of Industry and Advanced Technology (MoIAT). Confirm the current scheme with your importer before shipping.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-item">
      <h3>Do you supply batteries to the UAE?</h3>
      <p>Yes. DINWEYS exports JIS N150/N200 and DIN88/DIN100 heavy-duty batteries to UAE distributors, primarily through Jebel Ali Port in Dubai, with batch CCA test data and full shipping documentation on every delivery.</p>
    </div>

